<$fill $name="body">

!! Q: Why is nothing linked after a drop?

The plugin links nothing by itself. Add an action tiddler (see //Examples → Link the new tiddler to the drop target//).

!! Q: I dropped a Markdown file and got the import dialog.

On purpose: text files are tiddler content, not attachments, and go to the normal import. Only binary types are attached.

!! Q: Paste does nothing / says to select a tiddler.

Click into the tiddler you want to paste into (the thin bar on its left edge shows it is selected), then paste. The selected tiddler must be visible. A paste into a text editor is left to the editor.

!! Q: Does it need a server?

No. The file is stored in the wiki. On a Node.js server wiki TiddlyWiki saves it as a real file next to its `.meta`; in a single-file wiki it stays embedded until you extract it.

!! Q: My file type is attached as application/octet-stream.

TiddlyWiki does not know it. Add a line `<mime type> <.extension>` to `$:/config/rimir/drop-attach/extra-types` and restart.

!! Q: Can I drop on something other than story tiddlers?

Yes: tag a tiddler <<tag "$:/tags/rimir/drop-attach/target">> with a `selector` and the `title-attribute` that holds the title (see //Reference → Drop targets//).

</$fill>
